	"title": "A cache key as a pin lock",
	"label": "Pin-tumbler lock cut open on a footed base: eight pin stacks (spring, driver, pointed key pin) stand in the V cuts of a zigzag key blade, split at a dashed shear line; towers, hex-bolted brackets, face plate, fieldKey bow, draw counter.",
	"caption": "A pin-tumbler lock cut open. The key has one cut per shape setting, and the cache only opens when every cut still matches the last frame's: change one and its pin rides past the shear line, the lock jams and the frame redraws.",
